ons/github/test_integration.py","line":388,"severity":"medium","category":"test_gap","title":"test_installation_not_found no longer tests the installation-not-found path","body":"The assertion changed from \"The GitHub installation could not be found.\" to \"Invalid installation request.\", and a state-based callback request was added. The test now hits the generic invalid-request error (a state/pipeline mismatch) and never reaches `build_integration`'s 404 handling. The 404 stub is no longer exercised, so the behavior it was written for is untested. The test name is also misleading."},{"file":"tests/sentry/integrations/github/test_integration.py","line":399,"severity":"low","category":"test_gap","title":"No positive test for matching user, wrong state, or failed token exchange","body":"New tests cover only the mismatching-user case. There is no test where an existing Integration with a sender matches the OAuth user and the install succeeds. There is no test for a `state` mismatch, for a failed `access_token` exchange, or for a missing `sender` in metadata. In the success flows the Integration doesn't exist yet, so the comparison branch is never exercised. `assert_setup_flow` also relies on the brittle index `responses.calls[2]`."}]}
